[resource]
script = ExtResource("1")
title = "Combat"
brief_tooltip = "Ctrl + Left-click to attack with Officers/Captain.
Men defend themselves automatically.
Weapons matter — hatchets hit hardest."
detailed_text = "[b]Fighting for Survival[/b]

[i]Polar bears and wolves were a constant threat to the real expedition. Weakened, starving men travelling alone across the ice were easy prey. Those who carried weapons had a chance. Those who did not were found months later, bones scattered across the shingle.[/i]

The arctic is not empty. Polar bears patrol their territory and will attack intruders. Your men must be ready to fight — or to run.

[b]How to Attack[/b]

Select an [b]Officer[/b] or the [b]Captain[/b], then [b]Ctrl + Left-click[/b] on a hostile target. The unit will move into range and engage.

[b]Men[/b] cannot be ordered to attack. They will defend themselves automatically when something hits them, but they will not charge into danger on command.

[b]Weapons[/b]

What a man is carrying determines how well he fights:
• [b]Hatchet[/b] — The best melee weapon. Heavy hits, can sever limbs
• [b]Knife[/b] — Faster but weaker. Still far better than bare fists
• [b]Unarmed[/b] — A desperate last resort. Fists alone will not save a man from a bear

[b]Health & Wounds[/b]

Health bars appear above units in combat. Repeated blows — especially from large animals — can sever limbs. A man who loses a leg can only crawl. A man who loses his head does not get back up.

Wounded survivors bleed and need time to recover. Get them to shelter and safety.

[b]Fleeing[/b]

Badly wounded men will try to flee from danger. If they cannot escape, they will eventually turn and fight with whatever strength remains.

[b]Tips[/b]

• Travel in groups — a man caught alone by a polar bear has little chance
• Keep hatchets and knives distributed among your officers
• Do not send unarmed men to fight; order them to retreat instead
• After a fight, check your men's health and get the wounded to shelter"
